# J2r: the TP2 reference for J2 - the same image on the pair, general at two links, the same agreement prompts
# A committed TEMPLATE of .github/c2-serving-job.env for the TP4 bring-up (scripts/ci/c2_serving_job.py parses it):
# copy it over .github/c2-serving-job.env, commit, and push a tag experiment/c2-serving-vN. Nothing here names a rig,
# a card or a registry: the cards are resolved at run time.
# Duration (estimate, wall clock; the workflow's step limits in parentheses): smoke 25-50 min (engine build 10-20 min, cached), agreement 5-10 min: about 30-60 min; plus Jr before it.
# Push Jr (the four-card reset) first and this straight after it: no reset action here, because a pair-only reset
# leaves the pair's links to the other two boards untrained. general-2link is general under a two-channel pair
# descriptor: upstream's p150_x2 declares four channels and STRICT_INIT refuses the open when M-A trains two.
# Compare J2 against this file with tp_agreement.py compare: both collect the same prompts from the same checkout (each
# prompt's sha256 is stored, and a mismatch is NOT_COMPARABLE), so the tag pushed for J2 must carry the same
# scripts/ci/tp_agreement.py, tp4_mesh.py, c2_serving_gate.py and docs the tag of J2r did, or the prompts differ.
C2_ACTIONS=smoke
C2_IMAGE_TAG=tp4-1
C2_PROFILE=general-2link
C2_SMOKE_TESTS=warmup,coding,long_real_text,concurrent4,tool_call,stream_dropped,agreement
